n arrows  they're quite different  but if you look at the level above the  object level  all those vectors are the same  and of course  in an engineered system i want to  replicate the neural nets in every  location so i use exactly the same top  down in modern neural nets everywhere  and so the question is how can the same  neural net  be given a black arrow  and sometimes produce a red arrow and  sometimes produce a green arrow which  have quite different orientations  how can it produce  a nose where there's nose and a mouth  where there's max even though the face  vector is the same everywhere  and the answer is  the top-down neural network doesn't just  get  the face vector it also gets the  location of the patch for which is  producing  the part vector  so the three patches that should get the  red vector are different from the  different locations from the three  patches that should get the green vector  so if i use the neural network that gets  the location as input as well  here's what it can do  it can take the pose that's encoded in  that black vector the pose of the face  it can take the location  in the image  for which is predicting the vector of  the level below  and the pose is relative to the image  too so knowing the location in the image  and knowing the pose of the whole face  it can figure out which bit of the face  it needs to predict at that  location  and so in one location you can predict  okay there should be nose there and it  gives you the rib vector in another  location it can predict from where that  image patch is there should be mouth  there so it can give you the green arrow  so you can get the same vector at the  level above to predict different vectors  in different places level below by  giving it the place that it's predicting  for and that's what's going on in neural  fields  okay  um  now this was quite a complicated talk  there's a long paper about it on archive  that goes into much more detail  um and you could view this talk as just  an encouragement to read that paper  when i'm done  exactly on time  okay thank you so great thanks a lot  you
 

